lld/library-management.reference:
```mermaid
classDiagram
  class Book { isbn title authors }
  class BookCopy { id status }
  class Member { id name loans }
  class Loan { copy member dueDate returnedAt }
  class Reservation { book member }
  class Library { +borrow(member, copy) Loan +return(loan) Fine +reserve(member, book) }
  class FinePolicy { <<interface>> +fine(loan, returnDate) Money }
  class Notifier { <<interface>> +notify(member, message) }
  Book "1" o-- "*" BookCopy
  Member "1" o-- "*" Loan
  Loan --> BookCopy
  Library --> FinePolicy
  Library --> Notifier
  Library ..> Reservation
```

- `Library` coordinates; `Loan` holds the dates; a returned copy checks the title's reservation queue and tells the first member through `Notifier` (observer).
- `FinePolicy` is a strategy (per-day rate, capped fine, free for staff).
- A member's loan limit is checked in `borrow`, not scattered through callers.
